            <div xml:id="d302">

                <pb facs="0333" n="268" sameAs="frus:frus1936v03/pg268"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">701.4184/30: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister Resident in Ethiopia</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Engert</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Addis
                                Ababa</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1936-05-27T11:00:00+03:00">May 27, 1936—11
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received 4:37 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>374. Legation’s 334, May 12,<anchor n="32" xml:id="d302-f1"/> and Department’s
                    227, May 14. I learn that British and French Governments have both declined to
                    comply with Italian request that their respective legation guards be withdrawn
                    as they do not yet consider local situation sufficiently settled to warrant
                    it.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Engert</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
